  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES.\n\nCode (unchanged in mechanism since filing; 12 commits touched the file since 06-07, none in topic extraction):\n- linkers/message_queue.py:291-311 _extract_topic_from_match returns (identifier, \"variable\") for a non-literal arg; nothing resolves it.\n- :106 MessageQueuePattern.topic is documented \"literal value or variable name\"; :478-480 copies it into Symbol meta topic/topic_type; :528-534 joins publishers to subscribers on the raw (queue_type, topic) string.\n- :558-561/:588 edge-level topic_type is \"variable\" if EITHER end is variable -- so the same publisher's edges carry literal or variable depending on which subscriber it joined (the item's fan-out claim, by mechanism).\n\nRepro (scratch fixture, link_message_queues called directly): pub.py `EVENTS_TOPIC = \"orders\"; producer.produce(EVENTS_TOPIC, msg)` plus `producer.produce(\"orders\", msg)`; sub.py `consumer.subscribe([\"orders\"])`.\n  SYM kafka:publish:EVENTS_TOPIC  topic=EVENTS_TOPIC topic_type=variable\n  SYM kafka:publish:orders        topic=orders       topic_type=literal\n  EDGE only literal publish(7) -> subscribe(2); the variable publish gets NO edge.\nSo the variable publisher is unmatched against its literal subscriber, as filed.\n\nUpdates for the item:\n- SAME MECHANISM IN TWO SIBLING LINKERS, not named in the item: linkers/ipc.py:305-323 (_extract_channel_from_match, channel_type \"variable\") and linkers/event_sourcing.py:132-138 (event_type \"variable\"). Rule 3: the fix (resolve a module-level string constant, or label the value unresolved) is a shared helper, not a message_queue.py edit.\n- Related open row, cite not fold: WI-vovob (meta.channel duplicates meta.topic on event_publishes edges).\n- Not re-measured: the dogfood frequency / severity 3/5."  # 4ab6
